+## Launch and staging controls
 
-Set `DINAMICA_PUBLIC_LAUNCH=true` only after JJM and BCIE communications approval. Set `DINAMICA_APPLICATIONS_OPEN=true` only after the application window is approved. Final form access also requires `DINAMICA_PRIVACY_APPROVED=true`, an approved `DINAMICA_PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL`, `DINAMICA_DUPLICATE_POLICY_APPROVED=true`, Supabase server credentials, and `DINAMICA_OPERATOR_TOKEN`. All values default to closed or empty. Preview deployments remain `noindex` and the public sitemap excludes the route until the public launch flag is true.
+The public release is one coordinated state. Set `DINAMICA_PUBLIC_LAUNCH=true`, `DINAMICA_HOME_PROMOTION_ENABLED=true`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_DINAMICA_PUBLIC_LAUNCH=true`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_DINAMICA_HOME_PROMOTION_ENABLED=true`, and `DINAMICA_APPLICATIONS_OPEN=true` together only after institutional approval and launch readiness. The two `NEXT_PUBLIC_` values are public build-time mirrors used only by the client-rendered Home banner; they contain no secrets. `DINAMICA_LAUNCH_READY` also requires `DINAMICA_PRIVACY_APPROVED=true`, `DINAMICA_DUPLICATE_POLICY_APPROVED=true`, an approved `DINAMICA_PRIVACY_NOTICE_URL`, the dedicated Supabase server credentials, and `DINAMICA_OPERATOR_TOKEN`. Every public control defaults to off. The route stays not found, the route is omitted from the public sitemap, indexing is disabled, the Home banner is hidden, and the existing event-update popup remains active until the coordinated launch state is ready.
 
-The home banner component is prepared but intentionally not mounted on the homepage.
+Staging access is separate. On a Vercel Preview deployment protected by Vercel Deployment Protection, explicitly set `DINAMICA_PREVIEW_ENABLED=true`. Set `DINAMICA_PREVIEW_FORM_ENABLED=true` to test drafts and submissions, and `DINAMICA_PREVIEW_MODAL_ENABLED=true` to review the competition popup. The application and privacy prerequisites still apply. Do not enable these preview flags in Production. Preview pages remain `noindex`; public campaign flags stay false during QA.
+
+The Home promotion component is mounted in the existing Home layout, but renders only when `DINAMICA_LAUNCH_READY` is true. The root layout selects exactly one modal: the existing event update before launch, then the DINAMICA II competition announcement after launch approval (or explicitly in protected preview for review). The new modal uses its own session key.
 
